       generic _f_a_n_o_t_i_f_y___e_v_e_n_t___m_e_t_a_d_a_t_a structure.  This structure  is  defined
       as follows:

           struct fanotify_event_info_header {
                __u8 info_type;
                __u8 pad;
                __u16 len;
           };

       For  performance  reasons, it is recommended to use a large buffer size
       (for example, 4096 bytes), so that multiple events can be retrieved  by
       a single rreeaadd(2).

       The  return  value  of  rreeaadd(2)  is  the  number of bytes placed in the
       buffer, or -1 in case of an error (but see BUGS).

       The fields of the _f_a_n_o_t_i_f_y___e_v_e_n_t___m_e_t_a_d_a_t_a structure are as follows:

